    /// Given a positive 8-bit signed integer `n` (at least 1),
    /// returns the minimum number of banknotes/coins (denominations
    /// 100, 20, 10, 5, 1) needed to make exactly `n`.
    ///
    /// We prove that the result is non-negative and equals the canonical
    /// decomposition:
    ///   floor(n/100)
    /// + floor((n%100)/20)
